                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "42628890",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561197993459851",
                            "num_reviews": 31,
                            "playtime_forever": 173,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 173,
                            "last_played": 1528646183
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Pro's\n+ It looks like Sanitarium\n+ Quite impressive it's been made by a one man team\n+ One of few games to tackle taboo subjects\n+ Hellraiser, Jacobs Ladder flavours included\n+ Charming old school graphics\n+ Gory as hell\n+ No glitches/bugs (on my playthrough)\n\nCon's\n- It's not Sanitarium\n- Pricey for what you get\n- Don't care about whoever I'm even playing\n- Cringey dialogue and delivery\n- Majority of key items are practially invisible\n- Lose the cubase metal drums, the score is fine without them\n-  It can be a bit of a 'trench coat mafia/white knight simulator' at times (murderous hero, saving topless women)\n- Above mentioned taboo subjects are executed quite tastelessly (I had no idea Auschwitz was just filled with well fed female models. Also - saying \"poor people\" repeatedly doesn't give your character empathy)\n-  Finding a bic lighter in a concentration camp\n\n\n\nI really wanted to like this game, but it's a little too 'edgelord', and feels like somebody just threw lots of really interesting horror ideas together, with no real narrative. Hopefully it will be a thumbs up after updates/next chapters!",
                        "timestamp_created": 1528637763,
